Hi,

Review of `0001-ctlv-Add-the-schema-language-and-generator.patch`. Comments inline.

> From 8cc66fa0c3f4d7b33b42ba9ff44c9cb634c30c61 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
> From: Jiri Pirko <jiri@nvidia.com>
> Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 16:50:34 +0200
> Subject: [PATCH 01/20] ctlv: Add the schema language and generator
>
> Define the YAML schema and append-only family registry. Add ctlvgen to
> validate specifications and emit kernel and UAPI outputs.

The commit message undersells and misdescribes the patch. Besides "validate
specifications and emit kernel and UAPI outputs" it adds an ABI snapshot
compatibility checker (`compat.py`), a registry baseline, whole-tree coverage
checks (`tree.py`), an output-manifest reconciler (`outputs.py`), a Makefile, a
regeneration script and what looks like a userspace-binding name table.
None of the design (why a new schema language, the inheritance model, the
ABI rules the checker enforces) is explained, and there is no Documentation/
.rst at all: the YAML meta-schema is the only documentation.

Bisectability: this patch adds a Makefile and `ctlv-regen.sh` that operate on
`Documentation/ctlv/specs/*.yaml`, `Documentation/ctlv/families.yaml`,
`Documentation/ctlv/abi/` and `Documentation/ctlv/generated-files.yaml`. None of
those exist until a later patch (git ls-files at HEAD shows them added by the
root-family patch). With only this patch applied "make -C `tools/ctlv`" silently
does nothing (empty $(wildcard)) and `ctlv-regen.sh` fails on a missing
`ctlv.yaml`. The tool cannot be exercised, let alone tested, at this commit.

Nothing in this series adds a test: `outputs.py` refers to
`tools/ctlv/tests/specs` and `tests/generated-files.yaml`, and the docstrings in
`errors.py`, `sizes.py` and `cgen.py` say "a test checks that" / "the test suite
matches diagnostics", but `tools/ctlv/tests` does not exist at HEAD. Either
add the tests or drop the references (see inline comments).

