This says pre-post "reaches neither UAPI nor op-schema introspection", but
`compat.py` records "pre-post" in the ABI snapshot (`_ops`/`_compact_op`/
`_expand_ops`) and `_compare_ops()` reports a change of it as an ABI
incompatibility. Flipping a purely kernel-internal hook flag therefore
forces an "ABI" snapshot update and is reported as a break. Either the
property is ABI or it is not; the two documents disagree.

