General: many limits are enforced three times - here (minimum/maximum/
maxItems/maxLength), again in `spec.py` (`_max_occurrences`, `_u32_value`,
`_integer_bounds` scale range, `_blob` ranges, `_family_name` length, registry
size) and again in `semantics.py` (`_check_count` against `U16_MAX`/`U32_MAX`,
`MAX_FLAG_BITS`). After jsonschema validation succeeds, e.g. `value < 0` in
`_u32_value()`, "value < 1 or value > `U32_MAX`" in `_max_occurrences()` and
`_family_name()`'s length test cannot fire. Pick one place per rule. (The per-kind min/max narrowing in `_integer_bounds()` is not
redundant: the schema accepts the full -2^63..2^64-1 range for both kinds.)

