    """Run the CTLV schema tool and return its process exit status.

    Parses the command line, rejects invalid flag combinations through
    parser.error() (which exits with status 2 by itself), builds the spec.Paths
    for --spec and dispatches on exactly one action. --spec is always required;
    --schema, --registry and --abi are derived from it when not given.

    The actions fall in two groups. The whole-tree actions (--tree-check,
    --tree-check-update, --registry-abi-update, --outputs-check and
    --outputs-update) work from the family registry and the output manifests and
    return as soon as they are done, without loading the family named by --spec.
    --outputs-update runs tree.check_for_update() first and then rewrites the
    generated files; it prints one "ctlvgen: ..." line per change to standard
    error. --registry-abi-update requires complete ABI snapshots
    (tree.finish_update()) before it overwrites the registry ABI snapshot.

    The remaining actions load the single family with semantics.load() and then
    validate it (--validate), compare it with its ABI snapshot and the registry
    baseline (--abi-check), rewrite its ABI snapshot (--abi-update), or generate
    one uapi or kernel file (--mode with --header or --source). Generated text goes
    to standard output unless -o/--output is given.

    Only CtlvError is caught: it is printed as "ctlvgen: <message>" on standard
    error and turned into status 1. Any other exception propagates as a crash.
    The spec.Paths constructor runs outside the try block.

    Returns:
      int: 0 on success, 1 when a CtlvError was reported.

    Throws:
      SystemExit: through argparse, when the arguments are malformed or the
        combination of options is invalid (status 2).
    """

