`symbols()` is used as a validation pass whose returned table is thrown away by
every caller, and it is re-run from `gen_uapi.render()`, `gen_kernel.render_header()`
and `gen_kernel.render_source()` (so three times per family on `--outputs-`*),
plus once more via `--validate`. The name is misleading for what is really
`check_symbol_collisions()`. It also does not cover collisions between
different families that end up in one kernel image (only the "pre/post",
`_schema`, `_family` names of the chain), though a comment above claims
built-in families share one namespace.

