    """Emit the struct ctlv_family descriptor of a family, and export it.

    Appends to writer, in order: a one-line comment (root-family wording for
    the core family, "used by ctlv_create()" for any other), the definition
    of the descriptor, and an EXPORT_SYMBOL_NS_GPL() line for it. No trailing
    blank line is written. The emitted text looks like this, with the
    optional members present only when the family has them:

      /* Family descriptor used by ctlv_create(). */
      const struct ctlv_family tdx_family = {
              .schema = &tdx_schema,
              .parent = &ctlv_family,
              .ops = tdx_ops,
              .ops_count = ARRAY_SIZE(tdx_ops),
              .pre = tdx_op_pre,
              .post = tdx_op_post,
              .priv_size = tdx_priv_size,
              .init = tdx_init,
              .fini = tdx_fini,
              .stub_ops = tdx_stub_ops,
              .stub_ops_count = ARRAY_SIZE(tdx_stub_ops),
      };
      EXPORT_SYMBOL_NS_GPL(tdx_family, "CTLV");

    .schema always points at the schema node emitted by gen_kernel.
    .parent is the direct parent's descriptor (see _parent_descriptor) and
    is omitted only for the root family. .ops and .ops_count are emitted
    only if bindings(family) is non-empty, so they name the array written by
    _bindings (local actions and queries, never events or inherited ops).
