Undocumented and non-trivial: one routine handles two kinds with different
numbering rules and different limit checks, including an extra limit that
applies only to certain root-family enums. Suggested docstring:

    """Add one family's enum or flags definitions to the effective table.

    Called by _add_family once with the family's enums (kind 'enum') and once
    with its flags (kind 'flags'). Enum and flags names share one namespace, so
    a name already present from this or any ancestor family is rejected. Value
    numbering is assigned from declaration position: enum values start at 1
    because 0 is reserved, flag bits start at 0. Limits: a flags definition may
    have at most MAX_FLAG_BITS bits; an enum at most spec.U32_MAX values, and
    an enum of the root family (spec.CORE_FAMILY_ID) named in
    ROOT_ENUM_VALUES_MAX gets that tighter limit because it is stored in a
    narrower field.

