Correctness: PyYAML's SafeLoader implements YAML 1.1 scalar resolution
even though every file here starts with "%YAML 1.2" (PyYAML only checks the
major version). Unquoted on/off/yes/no/y/n resolve to booleans and 010, 1:20
to ints. Since names are kebab-case strings, an enum value or attr named
"on", "off", "yes" or "no" is loaded as a bool and rejected by the schema with
an unhelpful "False is not of type 'string'". "Strict YAML subset" should
reject these (override the bool/int resolvers) or the docs should say that
such names are unusable.

